  "simulation": {
    "tier": "none",
    "status": "not-modelled-yet",
    "what_it_models": [
      {
        "en": "Nothing runs in the Studio yet. The page lists the limits of the board, its seven faults and the truth table of one channel for reading."
      }
    ],
    "not_modelled": [
      {
        "en": "The two H-bridges: drive, brake and coast, with the enable as a duty from 0 to 1."
      },
      {
        "en": "The voltage lost in the switches, which the figure fits to the datasheet typical totals at 1 A and 2 A."
      },
      {
        "en": "The 5V-EN regulator, and the over-voltage and under-voltage thresholds the board is known to have."
      },
      {
        "en": "Heat in the chip and the overtemperature cut-out."
      },
      {
        "en": "Motor back-EMF, inductance and the flyback current through the eight diodes."
      },
      {
        "en": "Switching loss, PWM frequency limits, ripple, damage above 2 A and any current limit."
      },
      {
        "en": "The analog level on the inputs, clone chips and part-to-part variation."
      }
    ],
    "mocked": [
      {
        "en": "The overtemperature cut-out is a timer: with the stall fault set, the outputs switch off for 2 s of every 5 s once 6 s have passed."
      }
    ],
    "validity": [
